{
  "about": "Install steps run as Nextflow tasks by workflows/install.nf. A step with a module runs as its own process (modules/local/install_steps/MODULE, process NAME, or the process named in process when several steps share it): the tools' own commands and priva write its results into the task's data/ folder, and priva install-task record writes its receipt; storeDir keeps both in the step's lineage folder. stage: keys of the steps it needs whose files are staged into such a task. Any other step calls existing installer functions from scripts/install_utils.sh with its own private configuration, whose cache_root is the step's lineage folder. Tokens: {config} is that configuration, {script_dir} the scripts folder, {KEY} the configuration value of KEY. runs: installer functions that a program of the step runs itself (priva clinvar-gene-refresh runs the ClinVar stages), counted in the step's code digest with the functions its calls reach. needs: steps whose receipts supply input keys. outputs: keys the step must set; optional_outputs may be empty. user_inputs: keys naming files you supply, kept from your configuration and counted in lineage. settings: configuration values that change results (glob patterns allowed). copies: input keys the step rewrites in place; the runner copies them into the step's own folder first. writable: the folder stays writable after the step (otherwise it is made read-only). priva_commands: priva commands the step runs that its functions pick at run time (\"${PRIVA_BIN}\" \"$command\"); the Rust files behind every priva command a step runs count in its code digest. release: how to ask a changing source for its current release (git: the commit of url and ref; http: the server's ETag, Last-Modified and size), part of the step's lineage. Tokens {grch} (GRCh37 or GRCh38) and {loftee_branch} (master or grch38) follow the assembly. adopt_paths: where an older installation that does not name an output key put that file, for --adopt ({KEY} from the old configuration). pinned: the release is kept in resource_root/pins.json and only checked again with --refresh STEP. max_age_months: a pinned release older than this many calendar months (from the day it was taken) is replaced by the current one.",
  "folder_keys": [
    "cache_root",
    "vep_cache_dir",
    "vep_plugins_dir",
    "vep_plugins_cachedir",
    "gnomad_vcf_dir",
    "clinvar_vcf_dir",
    "cadd_parent_dir",
    "cadd_base_dir",
    "loftee_parent_dir",
    "hpo_raw_dir",
    "gene_mechanism_cache_dir",
    "gene_mechanism_raw_dir",
    "gofcards_workdir",
    "pext_tissue_bw_dir"
  ],
